      "page_title": "Lazy Futures: Nothing Runs Until Polled",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Calling It Runs Nothing",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async fn` returns an anonymous type implementing `Future`",
            "Calling it runs zero user code — no body executes",
            "A future is a value, not a task: state built, work not done",
            "Side effects you expect at call time defer to the first poll"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let f = fetch(url);   // nothing happened yet",
            "let body = f.await;   // NOW it starts",
            "spawn(fetch(url));    // or runtime drives it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Versus Eager Worlds"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "JS / Go",
                "lines": [
                  "`Promise` is eager and hot",
                  "Constructed = already running",
                  "`go f()` starts immediately"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Rust",
                "lines": [
                  "Future is cold until polled",
                  "Needs an explicit executor",
                  "`.await` or `spawn` starts it"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Trait Core"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "fn poll(",
            "  self: Pin<&mut Self>,",
            "  cx: &mut Context<'_>,",
            ") -> Poll<Self::Output>;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Poll::Pending` = not done, will wake later",
            "`Poll::Ready(T)` = value produced, future finished"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Footguns"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Built But Never Used",
          "items": [
            "`#[must_use]`: unused implementer of Future that must be used",
            "Warning only — it compiles and does nothing",
            "Dropping a future mid-flight silently cancels it",
            "No code after the last poll ever runs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why Laziness Pays"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`timeout(select(a, b))` builds ONE state machine",
            "No per-combinator allocation — zero-cost composition",
            "`async { .. }` blocks are lazy too",
            "`async move { .. }` takes ownership of its captures"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule Of Thumb",
          "text": "A future is a recipe. The runtime is the cook. Written recipes feed nobody."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "enum Fetch {",
            "  Start { url: String },",
            "  AwaitingBody { resp: Response },",
            "  Done,",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Resume, Not Restart",
          "text": "A re-poll jumps straight to the saved variant. Code before the last await never runs twice."
        }
      ]
    },
