        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Classic Error"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "future cannot be sent between threads safely",
            "note: ... held across an await point",
            "`Rc<T>` or `RefCell<T>` across an await kills `Send`",
            "Reach for `Arc<T>` and `tokio::sync::Mutex` instead",
            "`std::sync::MutexGuard` is `!Send` — scope it or go async"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Send, Sync, 'static: Why It Yells",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "'static Misread"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`'static` does not mean lives forever",
            "It means borrows nothing from the caller",
            "Fix: clone the data, or move an `Arc` into the async block"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let cfg = Arc::clone(&cfg);",
            "tokio::spawn(async move {",
            "  serve(&cfg).await // owns it",
            "});"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "When It Cannot Be Send"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Non-`Send` work belongs on `spawn_local` inside a `LocalSet`",
            "Or on a dedicated current-thread runtime"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let local = LocalSet::new();",
            "local.run_until(async {",
            "  spawn_local(uses_rc()).await",
            "}).await; // !Send is fine"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Send Offenders"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Held across await",
            "Send?",
            "Swap for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Rc<T>`",
              "{red:no}",
              "`Arc<T>`"
            ],
            [
              "`RefCell<T>`",
              "{red:no}",
              "a `Mutex`"
            ],
            [
              "std `MutexGuard`",
              "{red:no}",
              "scope it"
            ],
            [
              "`Arc<Mutex<T>>`",
              "{green:yes}",
              "—"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Async In Traits"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Auto traits leak: no `impl Future + Send` on trait methods unaided",
            "`async fn` in traits (stable 1.75) has no `Send` bound",
            "Use `trait_variant` or `#[async_trait]` to get one",
            "`#[async_trait]` boxes it: one alloc, dynamic dispatch per call"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "#[trait_variant::make(Db: Send)]",
            "trait LocalDb {",
            "  async fn get(&self, k: u64)",
            "    -> Option<Vec<u8>>;",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "generates a Send twin trait Db"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Debug Trick",
          "items": [
            "`fn assert_send<T: Send>(_: T) {}`",
            "Call it on the future where it is built",
            "The error names the offending local, not the spawn site"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reading The Error"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "\"has type `Rc<..>` which is not `Send`\" — the culprit",
            "\"await occurs here\" — the suspend point it crosses",
            "\"is later dropped here\" — where its life ends"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Sync Matters Too",
          "items": [
            "`&T` is `Send` only if `T: Sync`",
            "`Arc<T>` is `Send` only if `T: Send + Sync`",
            "So `Arc<RefCell<T>>` still fails to spawn"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Scope It",
          "text": "A `{ }` block that ends before the await is the surest way to drop a `!Send` value."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "let hash = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(",
            "    move || argon2_hash(&pw) // ~100 ms",
            ").await?;"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
